1
00:00:02,800 --> 00:00:08,575
MARCUS: No, tell them nine sharp. I've got the deck, I've got the clicker. Brenda... today is MY day.

2
00:00:11,375 --> 00:00:12,075
LEONARD: Bless you.

3
00:00:12,683 --> 00:00:15,098
MARCUS: Sorry. No, the BLUE slides.

4
00:00:20,098 --> 00:00:21,395
MARCUS: ...Can I help you?

5
00:00:22,195 --> 00:00:23,773
LEONARD: I said, bless you.

6
00:00:24,773 --> 00:00:26,188
MARCUS: Yeah. I heard.

7
00:00:29,088 --> 00:00:29,788
LEONARD: That's it?

8
00:00:30,499 --> 00:00:32,153
MARCUS: Brenda, let me call you back.

9
00:00:32,853 --> 00:00:35,906
MARCUS: What's 'it'? What's the 'it' you're looking for?

10
00:00:36,406 --> 00:00:40,775
LEONARD: A blessing was extended. Customarily, there's an acknowledgment.

11
00:00:41,175 --> 00:00:44,249
MARCUS: It's a reflex! It's just a thing people say.

12
00:00:44,849 --> 00:00:50,957
LEONARD: I don't say things. I blessed you. I reached in, and I gave you some of mine.

13
00:00:51,657 --> 00:00:53,608
MARCUS: Well, I didn't ask for it.

14
00:00:54,008 --> 00:00:57,020
LEONARD: Nobody asks. That's what makes it a gift.

15
00:00:57,720 --> 00:01:01,588
MARCUS: Okay. Well. I'm good. I'm all set on blessings.

16
00:01:02,188 --> 00:01:03,817
LEONARD: So you don't want it.

17
00:01:04,317 --> 00:01:06,170
MARCUS: I don't NEED it.

18
00:01:11,370 --> 00:01:13,174
LEONARD: Then I'll be taking it back.

19
00:01:13,574 --> 00:01:16,244
MARCUS: You'll be... how do you take back a...

20
00:01:22,544 --> 00:01:23,613
LEONARD: Un-bless you.

21
00:01:27,413 --> 00:01:30,540
MARCUS: Wow. Okay. Devastating.

22
00:01:35,140 --> 00:01:35,840
MARCUS: Really?

23
00:01:43,313 --> 00:01:45,138
MARCUS: ...That's a coincidence.

24
00:01:45,938 --> 00:01:48,939
LEONARD: Six letters. Hubris.

25
00:01:51,239 --> 00:01:57,326
MARCUS: Hey bud. Going with Greg for the presentation. Also, Greg's taking your office. Also, your chair.

26
00:01:57,726 --> 00:01:58,983
MARCUS: My CHAIR?

27
00:02:02,983 --> 00:02:05,904
MUM: Don't stare, darling. He's got no blessing.

28
00:02:06,404 --> 00:02:07,548
MARCUS: I'm FINE!

29
00:02:10,348 --> 00:02:11,924
MARCUS: Mom. Hey.

30
00:02:12,424 --> 00:02:21,472
MOM: Marcus, sweetheart. I don't know why, but I just had the strongest urge to call and tell you... I've always preferred your brother.

31
00:02:24,972 --> 00:02:28,262
MOM: Okay! Love you. Well... you know.

32
00:02:31,362 --> 00:02:34,781
MARCUS: Okay. Okay! Thank you. THANK you. There.

33
00:02:35,481 --> 00:02:36,181
LEONARD: For what?

34
00:02:36,875 --> 00:02:38,757
MARCUS: For... the bless you.

35
00:02:39,457 --> 00:02:41,038
LEONARD: You don't sound sure.

36
00:02:41,738 --> 00:02:45,774
MARCUS: Thank you for blessing me, sir, when I sneezed. Can I have it back?

37
00:02:46,574 --> 00:02:52,613
LEONARD: It's not that simple. The original was complimentary. This would be a re-blessing.

38
00:02:53,013 --> 00:02:54,044
MARCUS: What's the difference?

39
00:02:54,644 --> 00:02:55,433
LEONARD: Paperwork.

40
00:02:58,333 --> 00:03:02,517
LEONARD: In the past twelve months, have you declined any other courtesies?

41
00:03:03,417 --> 00:03:06,517
MARCUS: ...A guy held a door. I was on my phone.

42
00:03:07,117 --> 00:03:08,891
LEONARD: Mmm.

43
00:03:09,491 --> 00:03:10,800
MARCUS: What's 'mmm'?

44
00:03:11,300 --> 00:03:13,024
LEONARD: It's a pattern, Marcus.

45
00:03:13,924 --> 00:03:15,574
MARCUS: How do you know my name?

46
00:03:16,374 --> 00:03:17,585
LEONARD: It's on your lanyard.

47
00:03:19,885 --> 00:03:26,227
LEONARD: I'll need three thank-yous. One for the original. One for my time. And one in advance.

48
00:03:26,827 --> 00:03:28,502
MARCUS: Thank you. Thank you. Thank you.

49
00:03:29,102 --> 00:03:31,960
LEONARD: Those were to the pavement. In my eyes.

50
00:03:34,660 --> 00:03:35,360
MARCUS: Thank you.

51
00:03:38,644 --> 00:03:39,930
LEONARD: Was that so hard?

52
00:03:40,730 --> 00:03:42,798
MARCUS: So we're good. I'm re-blessed.

53
00:03:43,398 --> 00:03:46,724
LEONARD: Oh, I can't bless you. You'd have to sneeze.

54
00:03:49,224 --> 00:03:51,233
LEONARD: And my bus is in one minute.

55
00:03:55,033 --> 00:03:56,912
MARCUS: Ah... choo.

56
00:03:57,712 --> 00:04:01,348
LEONARD: I'm not blessing that. That was a man saying achoo.

57
00:04:13,148 --> 00:04:17,588
MARCUS: Wait, wait, wait! It's coming! Ah... AH... AAAH...

58
00:04:20,588 --> 00:04:21,532
MARCUS: ...I lost it.

59
00:04:22,432 --> 00:04:23,132
LEONARD: Mmm.

60
00:04:35,568 --> 00:04:36,313
LEONARD: ...Marcus.

61
00:04:41,513 --> 00:04:44,568
MARCUS: Brenda! Hey. No, no. Now's perfect.

62
00:04:58,368 --> 00:04:59,667
DENISE: Bless his heart.
